# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets and credentials
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. The deployment is designed so that no secret
# ever needs to live in a file here -- the Cloudflare tunnel token is held
# in a podman secret and injected as an env var at container start. These
# patterns are the backstop for the ways one turns up anyway: a .env copied
# from another stack (the Docker Compose flavour of this deployment used
# exactly that), a cloudflared credentials file, a stray key parked here.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
*.ppk
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
.netrc
_netrc
.npmrc
.pypirc
.htpasswd
credentials.json
*credentials.json
secrets.*
*.secret

# Deployment-local configuration. config.florun carries this host's UIDs,
# stack name and repo URL, and belongs in the WEBROOT (above the checkout)
# so a pull can never overwrite it -- this entry stops an accidental copy
# inside the checkout from being committed. The .example IS tracked, hence
# the negation.
config.florun
config.florun.local
!config.florun.example

# Updater output. Names host paths, deploy times, commit and image ids:
# noise in review, and more detail about the server than a public repo
# needs to carry.
*.log
update.log
update.log.*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Field data
#
# The whole point of the app is that measurements stay on the device.
# Exports cross that boundary by design -- one PDF carries GPS coordinates,
# the site label, free-text notes and an embedded photo -- so if a file gets
# saved into the project directory it must not follow anyone into a public
# repo. These match the filenames export.js actually writes.
FloRun-*.pdf
FloRun-*.csv
FloRun-History-*.pdf
FloRun-History-*.csv
history.json
history.corrupted-*.json
photos/
*.heic
*.HEIC

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# macOS
#
# This project lives on an external volume, where the OS scatters rather
# more of these than usual -- the volume root already carries
# .Spotlight-V100, .fseventsd, .TemporaryItems and friends.
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.TemporaryItems
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.VolumeIcon.icns
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent
.AppleDB
.AppleDesktop
Network Trash Folder
Temporary Items
.apdisk

# Windows / Linux, for anyone else who checks this out
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
.directory
.Trash-*
.nfs*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Editors, IDEs and agent tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
.*.sw?
*~
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
.zed/
.history/
.claude/
launch.json

# Merge, patch and backup leftovers
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak
*.tmp
*.temp

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tooling artefacts
#
# The app has no build step and no dependencies, so none of this should
# ever exist here -- but a stray command still creates it, and an
# accidental `npm install` would otherwise offer thousands of files up for
# staging.
node_modules/
bower_components/
.npm/
.yarn/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.Python
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Archives -- almost always a backup of the webroot, which would carry
# config.florun and update.log inside it.
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.rar
*.7z
